    crm:P129i_is_subject_of <https://mbdiaries.itatti.harvard.edu/diary/1916/document/20> ;
    crm:P183i_has_representation <https://ids.lib.harvard.edu/ids/iiif/493308911/full/full/0/default.jpg> ;
    rdf:value """Friday, January 14, I Tatti
Glorious. Warm   
Julia, Geoffrey Scott, Cecil Pinsent
(4 lunch 5 dinner) 
Prepared villino for Geoffrey’s pass: the scarlet fever. Lina came along and Gordon climbed on the roof with Julia. 
Had a long and glorious walk with B.B. over the Scavi to the very top and back by Fiesole. He went to see Sybil and I was picked up by Lady Enniskillen who brought me home. Sybil was still going on about  not  being self-absorbed, her very tenacity and volubility proving she was!
Geoffrey had a walk with Byba, who came in to tea and discussed common acquaintances.     He had a letter from Marcella Michela and wrote use! """^^xsd:string ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:index 20 ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:part_of <https://mbdiaries.itatti.harvard.edu/resource/diary/1916> .

